1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Welcome to the Local Knowledge Vault media demo.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,000
Captions become normal vault notes with timestamps.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Ask stays grounded and cites transcript chunks with itm_ ids.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,500
When you click a citation, the player seeks to that moment.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Follow playhead narrows chat to nearby cues for about forty five seconds.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
This second stretch keeps talking so chunking can group cues into longer notes around thirty to sixty seconds.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Chunk boundaries prefer time windows and character budgets without splitting a single cue across notes.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
YouTube ingest uses yt-dlp when available; local SRT and VTT always work end to end.
